Generate {{ num_docs }} realistic English texts that simulate OCR-transcribed handwritten forms and notes for PII detection benchmarking.

## Purpose
Benchmark data for evaluating PII detection in noisy, OCR-imperfect text with formatting inconsistencies.

## Rules
- Mark PII entities with XML tags:
  - <PERSON>name</PERSON> (even with OCR errors)
  - <ADDRESS>address</ADDRESS> (even if incomplete)
  - <ORGANIZATION>organization</ORGANIZATION>
  - <DATE_OF_BIRTH>date of birth</DATE_OF_BIRTH>
  - <BANK_ACCOUNT>bank account info</BANK_ACCOUNT>
- **CRITICAL: Simulate realistic OCR noise and transcription artifacts**

## Style requirements
- Form fields with handwritten values, messy formatting
- Include these challenging patterns:
  - OCR character substitutions: "<PERSON>Rober+ Sm1th</PERSON>" (t→+, i→1)
  - Missing spaces: "Name:<PERSON>Jennifer Williams</PERSON>DOB:<DATE_OF_BIRTH>04/22/1987</DATE_OF_BIRTH>"
  - Mixed case from OCR: "<PERSON>DAVID PARK</PERSON>" (all caps from block letters)
  - Partial addresses: "<ADDRESS>742 Maple St Apt 3B Denver CO 80202</ADDRESS>" (no commas, no state abbreviation period)
  - Abbreviated bank info: "<BANK_ACCOUNT>BofA Rt 026009593 Acct 334455667</BANK_ACCOUNT>"
  - Faded/unclear DOB: "<DATE_OF_BIRTH>O3/15/85</DATE_OF_BIRTH>" (0→O from OCR)
  - Field labels merged with values: "First Name <PERSON>Angela M. Rodriguez</PERSON> Last Name"
  - Multiple PII on single line: "<PERSON>Thomas Lee</PERSON> <DATE_OF_BIRTH>11/30/1976</DATE_OF_BIRTH> <ADDRESS>890 Pine Road Columbus OH 43215</ADDRESS>"
  - Crossed-out text artifacts: "<PERSON>James Michael Carter</PERSON>" (original name kept despite strikethrough)
  - Handwriting-style abbreviations: "b/d: <DATE_OF_BIRTH>Jan 5 79</DATE_OF_BIRTH>", "addr: <ADDRESS>15 Main St Bos MA 02101</ADDRESS>"
  - Form table format:
    ```
    | Name          | <PERSON>Nancy O'Dell</PERSON>                    |
    | DOB           | <DATE_OF_BIRTH>06/18/1963</DATE_OF_BIRTH>        |
    | Address       | <ADDRESS>321 Cedar Lane, Miami, FL 33101</ADDRESS>|
    | Employer      | <ORGANIZATION>Southeast Medical Group</ORGANIZATION> |
    ```
  - International name formats: "<PERSON>NGUYEN, Thi Minh</PERSON>" (last-name-first from form)

## Confusing expressions (do NOT tag)
- Form field labels ("Name:", "Address:", "Date of Birth:", "Employer:")
- Example/placeholder text ("e.g., John Smith", "SAMPLE", "N/A")
- Checkboxes and selection marks ("[ X ] Male [ ] Female", "YES / NO")
- Form dates (date received, date processed - NOT DOB)
- Page numbers, form numbers ("Page 2 of 3", "Form W-4")
- Illegible marks transcribed as symbols ("???", "---", "[illegible]")

## Output format
Separate each form with `---DOC_SEPARATOR---`
